A closed half-cylinder and a half-cylinder trough open along the top both have radius $2$ cm and length $9$ cm. Both have two semicircular ends.
Their end cross-section is shown; the diameter forms the closed solid's flat top and the trough's opening.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-2,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=360,radius=2];
\draw (-2,0)--(2,0);
\draw (0,0)--(0,-2);
\path (0,-1) node[right] {$2\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find both surface areas to $2$ decimal places. Explain what their difference represents.

A closed quarter-cylinder has radius $4$ cm and length $11$ cm. Its end cross-section is shown.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(2,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=90,radius=2]--cycle;
\draw (0.25,0)--(0.25,0.25)--(0,0.25);
\path (1,0) node[below] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find its surface area to $2$ decimal places.

A semicircular gutter is open along the top and at both ends. Its radius is $6$ cm and its length is $80$ cm.
The end profile is shown; there is no flat top or end plate.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-2,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=360,radius=2];
\draw[dotted] (0,0)--(0,-2);
\path (0,-1) node[right] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the area of material used, to $1$ decimal place. Ignore its thickness.
